{"id": "EUVD-2026-26641", "enisaUuid": "72fa7d2e-483c-3d5c-ba46-76d1fde0d1bd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmpls: add seqcount to protect the platform_label{,s} pair\n\nThe RCU-protected codepaths (mpls_forward, mpls_dump_routes) can have\nan inconsistent view of platform_labels vs platform_label in case of a\nconcurrent resize (resize_platform_label_table, under\nplatform_mutex). This can lead to OOB accesses.\n\nThis patch adds a seqcount, so that we get a consistent snapshot.\n\nNote that mpls_label_ok is also susceptible to this, so the check\nagainst RTA_DST in rtm_to_route_config, done outside platform_mutex,\nis not sufficient. This value gets passed to mpls_label_ok once more\nin both mpls_route_add and mpls_route_del, so there is no issue, but\nthat additional check must not be removed.", "datePublished": "2026-05-01T14:15:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:39:55", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0d377825548fe598595b5a5fa4a309fb593d8fb4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8adc5b6fc876928d8c95555d30b66fa50b07421e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5bb3caf0bbfb56f1a00d2af072ac3d8395a3b9ef", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/629ec78ef8608d955ce217880cdc3e1873af3a15"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-43042", "GHSA-j45g-66j9-q94m"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "12f70ed6-a255-3b10-8bb3-13b0d96fe05a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.12"}, {"id": "1ac39411-4811-36b0-bfed-aebc42954482", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "33c018a4-c3f8-3829-8aae-e8befc964987", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}, {"id": "69e5e368-159f-36ec-bfcc-324dea86d3a3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": 